    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> Splinters!

With Gallax isolated in the Freehold and unable to enforce unity through his principle of absolute leadership, the conflicting ideologies and ambitions within the movement have broken into open dispute. While Gallax continues to issue directives to [+ royalist_leader +] and [+ royalist_chancellor +], the failure of the all-or-nothing strategy is now blamed squarely on both. Increasingly withdrawn, Gallax has grown critical of the very men he once entrusted with power—though he keeps his discontent private.

Garrick Crowde, seeing the collapse of Standerton and Gorrick’s reckless course, has reconsidered. He now believes the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> movement still has a future—but only without the failed strategies of its current leadership. For the first time, Crowde is willing to defy the distant messiah in the Freehold and seize control.

The result is a formal split within the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>: pragmatists like Crowde, Frask, and even Glade now oppose the disastrous passivity of Standerton and Gorrick. To give their faction a political home, they have founded the <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">Commonwealth Social Union</span> (<span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**DSU**</span>), advocating a middle path—preparing for revolution, while participating in government to avoid total irrelevance.

- @nazi_2: Without funds and without support. 

@nazi_2
on-arrival: {!
Q.royalist_split = 1;
Q.dsu_exist = 1;
Q.dsu_leader = "Triumvirate";
Q.dsu_alt = 1;
Q.nvf_exist = 0;
Q.dsu_r = Math.round(Q.royalist_r*0.4 * 10) / 10;
Q.royalist_gallax_r = Math.round((Q.royalist_r - Q.dsu_r) * 10) / 10;
!}

The two parties are doomed to eternal infighting and, eventually, irrelevance. However, the polarization caused by this, coupled with the potential for participationist <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> entering the government, may still have far-reaching consequences.

We must not get complacent.